;spacing=0;tl=bar;zone=su_in;sig=应答;kind=on;fillColor=#a07800;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p5-sig"><mxGeometry x="633" y="284" width="43" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-89" value="Stable = 1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=7.5;spacing=0;tl=bar;zone=su_in;sig=应答;kind=on;fillColor=#a07800;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p5-sig"><mxGeometry x="1233" y="284" width="43" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-90" value="Stable" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=10.5;spacing=0;tl=bar;zone=su_st;sig=安定（内部）;kind=green;fillColor=#548235;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p5-sig"><mxGeometry x="883" y="314" width="448" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-91" value="Stable = 0" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=10.5;spacing=0;tl=bar;zone=plc;sig=缓存;kind=val;fillColor=#f8d7d7;strokeColor=#c00000;fontColor=#c00000;" vertex="1" parent="p5-sig"><mxGeometry x="633" y="344" width="598" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-92" value="Stable = 1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=10.5;spacing=0;tl=bar;zone=plc;sig=缓存;kind=val;fillColor=#f8d7d7;strokeColor=#c00000;fontColor=#c00000;" vertex="1" parent="p5-sig"><mxGeometry x="1233" y="344" width="98" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-93" value="[Notes]" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;fontColor=#111827;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p5-table"><mxGeometry x="10" y="388" width="200" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-94" value="※1 The cleaner reads every 500 ms; the PLC reads the heater every 3 s. The PLC answers the cleaner's reads from cache without waiting for the heater [P]." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#1f2937;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="p5-table"><mxGeometry x="14" y="410" width="1324" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-95" value="※2 After the heater status changes, the DO and read replies catch up at most 3 s later (here it becomes stable at 1.25 s and shows up only at 3.0 s). Requests and replies are drawn at the same moment: a normal round trip takes tens of ms." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#1f2937;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="p5-table"><mxGeometry x="14" y="430" width="1324" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-96" value="※3 Normally only the equipment status is read (run, inlet valve, stop / continue error, heating, flow, stable, serial mode, leak); the reply is a dozen-odd bytes [I]. Alarm detail is read only when a status error bit is set (reply 130+ bytes, about 0.15 s at 9600 bps), see 4-1 [P]." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#1f2937;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="p5-table"><mxGeometry x="14" y="468" width="1324" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p5-97" value="※4 Alarms are not drawn in this chart; see 4." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#1f2937;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="p5-table"><mxGeometry x="14" y="506" width="1324" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="chart-4-1" name="4-1 Heater alarm → major fault → reset"><mxGraphModel dx="1452" dy="866" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="0" arrows="0" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1452" pageHeight="866" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="p6-0"/><mxCell id="p6-table" value="Table" style="locked=1;" parent="p6-0"/><mxCell id="p6-sig" value="Signal" parent="p6-0"/><mxCell id="p6-1" value="4-1  Heater alarm → major fault → reset" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=18;fontColor=#1f3864;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="10" y="8" width="1432" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-2" value="This chart answers: When the heater raises an alarm, what does the cleaner see; what must the PLC finish within the 5 s reset signal?" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;fontColor=#374151;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="10" y="40" width="1432" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-3" value="Legend: [I] cleaner / heater side premise   [IO] IO assignment   [P] this PLC proposal   [?] not decided   [OK] decided   |   red dashed box &quot;none&quot; = no reply" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=10;fontColor=#6b7280;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=2;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="10" y="66" width="1432" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-4" value="Group" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;fillColor=#1f3864;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#ffffff;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="0" y="96" width="112" height="64" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-5" value="Signal" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;fillColor=#1f3864;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#ffffff;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="112" y="96" width="180" height="64" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-6" value="Notes" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;fillColor=#1f3864;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#ffffff;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="292" y="96" width="340" height="64" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-7" value="①" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=13;fillColor=#1f3864;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#ffffff;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="632" y="96" width="100" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-8" value="Supplying" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=10.5;fillColor=#dde4f0;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#1f2937;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="632" y="122" width="100" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-9" value="②" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=13;fillColor=#1f3864;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#ffffff;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="p6-table"><mxGeometry x="732" y="96" width="100" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="p6-10" value="Heater alarm" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=10.